            <title>[LU-9407] sanity-lfsck test_20b: MDS1 is not the expected "completed'' </title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-9407</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Doug Oucharek &amp;lt;doug.s.oucharek@intel.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.hpdd.intel.com/test_sets/fa0f7094-2a24-11e7-b742-5254006e85c2" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.hpdd.intel.com/test_sets/fa0f7094-2a24-11e7-b742-5254006e85c2&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sub-test test_20b failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;(4) MDS1 is not the expected 'completed'
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Many of the tests in the sanity-lfsck set which followed this one failed.  I am assuming this first failure triggered all the others (so won't create any additional tickets).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please provide additional information about the failure here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Info required for matching: sanity-lfsck 20b&lt;/p&gt;</description>
